erdict:</strong> Neither. A daily close above $121.87 would put the chart behind the upside; a daily close under $116.66 would say the rebound has failed. That fits what management described: strong revenue, profit capped by fuel.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>Fuel: Brent holding under $90 with the Strait calm, or back above $110.</li><li>A daily close above $121.87 or below $116.66.</li><li>The next report (date not found; Q4 results will show whether fares kept pace with $4.80 fuel).</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>High on reported results and Q4 guidance. Medium-low on call colour and the full-year comparison: no full transcript could be opened and those points rest on AI-assisted summaries. One of them puts the full year at roughly $6.20 to $7.20 against $9 to $11 in July; treat the direction (a cut) as solid and the figures as soft. People facts come from an executive-listing page, not a company filing.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://finviz.com/news/404790/united-delivers-record-17-revenue-growth-in-q3-and-expects-record-q4-revenue-growth-underpinned-by-accelerating-customer-investments\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Press release copy (Finviz)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.airwaysmag.com/new-post/united-record-q3-revenue-fuel-costs-2026\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Airways Magazine</a></li><li><a href=\"https://viewfromthewing.com/united-airlines-reports-earnings-record-revenue-but-delta-made-35-more-profit-on-lower-sales/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View from the Wing</a></li><li><a href=\"https://finviz.com/news/405689/united-airlines-narrowly-misses-as-record-revenue-collides-with-a-fuel-shock-that-guts-the-full-year-outlook\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Earnings Whispers article (AI-assisted)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://stockhub.kr/en/insights/ual-cy2026-q3-earnings-call-20261020\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"